@anon.9bf146a73cb71d9c7e3fe69f46c42f4a.477 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [897 x i8] }> <{ [897 x i8] c"Determines the location of an element in the document.\0A\0ATakes a selector that must match exactly one element and returns that\0Aelement's [`location`]. This location can, in particular, be used to\0Aretrieve the physical [`page`]($location.page) number and\0A[`position`]($location.position) (page, x, y) for that element.\0A\0A# Examples\0ALocating a specific element:\0A```example\0A#context [\0A  Introduction is at: \\\0A  #locate(<intro>).position()\0A]\0A\0A= Introduction <intro>\0A```\0A\0A# Compatibility\0AIn Typst 0.10 and lower, the `locate` function took a closure that made the\0Acurrent location in the document available (like [`here`] does now).\0ACompatibility with the old way will remain for a while to give package\0Aauthors time to upgrade. To that effect, `locate` detects whether it\0Areceived a selector or a user-defined function and adjusts its semantics\0Aaccordingly. This behaviour will be removed in the future." }>, align 1
